  "id": "COMPOUND:34580 - PROTEIN:3707",
  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B appears to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the activation of Lantibiotic cinnamycin. The evidence suggests that Isoswinholide B acts as a target for several kinases, including NUAK family SNF1-like kinase 1, Tubulin beta-2A chain, and Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13. These targets are all involved in cellular processes that can influence the production or activity of Lantibiotic cinnamycin. The shared pathway involves the regulation of protein synthesis and cellular signaling, which may explain the indirect relationship between Isoswinholide B and Lantibiotic cinnamycin. The evidence supports a mechanism where Isoswinholide B modulates the activity of these targets, potentially influencing the biosynthesis of Lantibiotic cinnamycin. This integrated pathway highlights the role of these targets in the broader context of drug action and cellular regulation.",
